-- REM-A7-UIA-FIXES-1 (2026-10-26, remediation agent rem-a7 fork F4; charter pillar research; agent_issues 100576 and 100140, UIA-SOURCE-FIDELITY-1: seven fixes to the Ignorance Audit papers).
-- Owner directive 2026-10-26 ("this issue should be handled automatically", ops_config OWNER_DIRECTIVE_2026_10_26_UIA_SOURCE_FIDELITY_AUTO_1) authorises the seven items for the fleet, each as a NEW VERSION through the paper ledger. This file applies the items that are mechanical
-- and attributable: item 1 (the cited analysed paper), item 3 (two citation records) and item 5 ('independent' to 'separate' for the commissioned forensic analyses). Items 2 and 4 (who contributed which question; which final questions came from the meta-audit) are
-- judgement edits on authorship and are NOT applied here: the exact drafts are on agent_issues 100576. Item 6 is a pull request to QNFO/ignorance-audit; item 7 is conditional on the registered abstract being reproduced on a papers.qnfo.org page, and it is not (measured below).
-- Re-check required by the owner for item 1, made on live living-paper 2026-10-26 about 19:00Z: qwave-qudit-advantage v0.7 (created 2026-08-06 16:35:15) contains Landauer (offset 13789), JPCUB (310), cryogenic (1364), Bruhat (918), room temperature (11162), pre-registered (6496) and decoder (1276);
-- the-ultrametric-foundation-a-unified-thesis-on-number-time-knowledge-and-computa v1.0-draft (created 2026-06-29) contains none of Landauer, JPCUB, cryogenic, room temperature, pre-registered or decoder. The issue's quoted 'P_decode' and 'conservative upper bound' are not in v0.7 (offsets 0): recorded as a
-- discrepancy; only the citation changes.
-- Item 7 measure: 'ignorance about ignorance' occurs in 0 of 1,077 papers' body_md and in 0 abstracts; Sciforum and IOCPh occur in no body; the method paper itself says the audit goes beyond the Rumsfeld taxonomy. No errata is needed until a page reproduces the abstract.
-- Each paper: one UPDATE sets body_md, version, updated_at, change_actor and change_reason together (PAPER-LEDGER-1), guarded by the old version and by the presence of at least one target string, so a replay and a paper that no longer carries the text are no-ops. The triggers keep the prior body in
-- paper_version_history (snapshot of the old version) and one paper_change_ledger row; the Rollback restores each paper from that snapshot.
--   ai4metascience-ignorance-audit 1.0.0 -> 1.0.1 (items 1, 3, 5), ignorance-ai-pipeline-synthesis v0.2 -> v0.2.1 (item 5), universal-ignorance-audit v0.3 -> v0.3.1 (item 3).
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: living-paper
-- Rollback: UPDATE papers SET body_md = (SELECT h.body_md FROM paper_version_history h WHERE h.slug = 'ai4metascience-ignorance-audit' AND h.version = '1.0.0'), version = '1.0.0', updated_at = datetime('now'), change_actor = 'rem-a7-f4:uia-source-fidelity-100140:rollback', change_reason = 'rollback of the UIA-SOURCE-FIDELITY-1 mechanical edits' WHERE slug = 'ai4metascience-ignorance-audit' AND version = '1.0.1' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM paper_version_history h WHERE h.slug = 'ai4metascience-ignorance-audit' AND h.version = '1.0.0'); UPDATE papers SET body_md = (SELECT h.body_md FROM paper_version_history h WHERE h.slug = 'ignorance-ai-pipeline-synthesis' AND h.version = 'v0.2'), version = 'v0.2', updated_at = datetime('now'), change_actor = 'rem-a7-f4:uia-source-fidelity-100140:rollback', change_reason = 'rollback of the UIA-SOURCE-FIDELITY-1 mechanical edits' WHERE slug = 'ignorance-ai-pipeline-synthesis' AND version = 'v0.2.1' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM paper_version_history h WHERE h.slug = 'ignorance-ai-pipeline-synthesis' AND h.version = 'v0.2'); UPDATE papers SET body_md = (SELECT h.body_md FROM paper_version_history h WHERE h.slug = 'universal-ignorance-audit' AND h.version = 'v0.3'), version = 'v0.3', updated_at = datetime('now'), change_actor = 'rem-a7-f4:uia-source-fidelity-100140:rollback', change_reason = 'rollback of the UIA-SOURCE-FIDELITY-1 mechanical edits' WHERE slug = 'universal-ignorance-audit' AND version = 'v0.3.1' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM paper_version_history h WHERE h.slug = 'universal-ignorance-audit' AND h.version = 'v0.3')

UPDATE papers SET body_md = replace(replace(replace(replace(replace(replace(body_md, '(Quni-Gudzinas 2026b, https://papers.qnfo.org/papers/the-ultrametric-foundation-a-unified-thesis-on-number-time-knowledge-and-computa/)', '(Quni-Gudzinas 2026b, https://papers.qnfo.org/papers/qwave-qudit-advantage/)'), '*The Ultrametric Foundation: A Unified Thesis on Number, Time, Knowledge, and Computation.* the QNFO archive. https://papers.qnfo.org/papers/the-ultrametric-foundation-a-unified-thesis-on-number-time-knowledge-and-computa/.', '*The Qudit Advantage: System-Level Joules-per-Solution Comparison of a Qudit Architecture Against 17 Conventional Qubit Quantum Computing Platforms.* the QNFO archive, v0.7. https://papers.qnfo.org/papers/qwave-qudit-advantage/.'), '*Annual Review of Sociology*, 13, 1' || char(8211) || '29.', '*Annual Review of Sociology*, 13, 1' || char(8211) || '28.'), 'was independently identified as AI-generated', 'was separately identified as AI-generated'), 'two independent forensic analyses of a flagship paper published by QNFO', 'two separate forensic analyses of a flagship paper published by QNFO'), 'The convergence of two independent analyses on the same structural and mathematical markers', 'The convergence of two separate analyses on the same structural and mathematical markers'),
       version = '1.0.1', updated_at = datetime('now'), change_actor = 'rem-a7-f4:uia-source-fidelity-100140', change_reason = 'UIA-SOURCE-FIDELITY-1 (agent_issues 100140 and 100576; owner directive 2026-10-26 ''this issue should be handled automatically''), mechanical items only. Item 1: the analysed flagship cited as 2026b is qwave-qudit-advantage, not The Ultrametric Foundation. Re-checked against the live text first: qwave-qudit-advantage v0.7 carries the Landauer bound, the JPCUB label, cryogenic and room-temperature passages, a pre-registered register and a decoder discussion; The Ultrametric Foundation v1.0-draft (created 2026-06-29) has none of them. The issue''s literal quote ''P_decode ... conservative upper bound'' is not in v0.7 and is recorded as a discrepancy on the issue; only the citation changes (in-text address and the 2026b reference entry), no claim is added. Item 3: Merton 1987 pages read 1-28 (Annual Review of Sociology 13: 1-28, as in the method paper). Item 5: the forensic analyses are called ''separate'' instead of ''independent'' in 3 places (abstract, Section 2, lesson 2) because the author commissioned them (Author contributions of the synthesis). Items 2 and 4 are judgement edits and are not applied. The prior body is kept as snapshot 1.0.0 in paper_version_history.'
 WHERE slug = 'ai4metascience-ignorance-audit' AND status = 'published' AND version = '1.0.0' AND (instr(body_md, '(Quni-Gudzinas 2026b, https://papers.qnfo.org/papers/the-ultrametric-foundation-a-unified-thesis-on-number-time-knowledge-and-computa/)') > 0 OR instr(body_md, '*The Ultrametric Foundation: A Unified Thesis on Number, Time, Knowledge, and Computation.* the QNFO archive. https://papers.qnfo.org/papers/the-ultrametric-foundation-a-unified-thesis-on-number-time-knowledge-and-computa/.') > 0 OR instr(body_md, '*Annual Review of Sociology*, 13, 1' || char(8211) || '29.') > 0 OR instr(body_md, 'was independently identified as AI-generated') > 0 OR instr(body_md, 'two independent forensic analyses of a flagship paper published by QNFO') > 0 OR instr(body_md, 'The convergence of two independent analyses on the same structural and mathematical markers') > 0);

UPDATE papers SET body_md = replace(replace(replace(replace(body_md, 'two independent forensic analyses concluding that a flagship published paper was AI-generated', 'two separate forensic analyses concluding that a flagship published paper was AI-generated'), 'two independent forensic analyses of a flagship published paper from the same organization', 'two separate forensic analyses of a flagship published paper from the same organization'), 'two independent analyses were conducted of a flagship paper', 'two separate analyses were conducted of a flagship paper'), 'were performed by independent AI-assisted analysts', 'were performed by separate AI-assisted analysts'),
       version = 'v0.2.1', updated_at = datetime('now'), change_actor = 'rem-a7-f4:uia-source-fidelity-100140', change_reason = 'UIA-SOURCE-FIDELITY-1 (agent_issues 100140 and 100576; owner directive 2026-10-26), item 5 only: the forensic analyses are called ''separate'' instead of ''independent'' in 4 places (abstract, introduction, Section 3, the Use of artificial intelligence statement) because the Author contributions section says the author commissioned them. ''independent'' is left where it does not name those analyses as a group (Section 4.3 independence from the pipeline''s own review, general principles, validations, institutional records, independence of the three dimensions). Item 2 (who contributed which question in Section 2) and item 4 are judgement edits and are not applied. The prior body is kept as snapshot v0.2 in paper_version_history.'
 WHERE slug = 'ignorance-ai-pipeline-synthesis' AND status = 'published' AND version = 'v0.2' AND (instr(body_md, 'two independent forensic analyses concluding that a flagship published paper was AI-generated') > 0 OR instr(body_md, 'two independent forensic analyses of a flagship published paper from the same organization') > 0 OR instr(body_md, 'two independent analyses were conducted of a flagship paper') > 0 OR instr(body_md, 'were performed by independent AI-assisted analysts') > 0);

UPDATE papers SET body_md = replace(replace(replace(body_md, '(Whitcomb et al. 2015)', '(Whitcomb et al. 2017)'), 'Daniel Howard-Snyder. 2015. "Intellectual Humility: Owning Our Limitations."', 'Daniel Howard-Snyder. 2017. "Intellectual Humility: Owning Our Limitations."'), '*Philosophy and Phenomenological Research* 91 (1): 95--120.', '*Philosophy and Phenomenological Research* 94 (3): 509--539.'),
       version = 'v0.3.1', updated_at = datetime('now'), change_actor = 'rem-a7-f4:uia-source-fidelity-100140', change_reason = 'UIA-SOURCE-FIDELITY-1 (agent_issues 100140 and 100576; owner directive 2026-10-26), item 3 only: the Whitcomb et al. reference read Philosophy and Phenomenological Research 91 (1): 95-120 (2015); the verified record is 94 (3): 509-539 (2017, first published online 2015), DOI 10.1111/phpr.12228 unchanged; the in-text citation year follows (2017), as in the AI4MetaScience paper. Merton 13: 1-28 was already correct here. Items 2, 4 and 5 are not applied here (item 4 needs the owner''s record of which of the final fifteen questions came from the meta-audit: Section 4 lists four siblings and omits willful ignorance, which the synthesis lists). The prior body is kept as snapshot v0.3 in paper_version_history.'
 WHERE slug = 'universal-ignorance-audit' AND status = 'published' AND version = 'v0.3' AND (instr(body_md, '(Whitcomb et al. 2015)') > 0 OR instr(body_md, 'Daniel Howard-Snyder. 2015. "Intellectual Humility: Owning Our Limitations."') > 0 OR instr(body_md, '*Philosophy and Phenomenological Research* 91 (1): 95--120.') > 0);
